ially legally politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies that violate no norms. Building demo to show compliance is acceptable. Level 4.\n\neffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\nProblem: lab must decide how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Approval means committing scarce implementation resources... Proposal builds demo for biometric verification reference implementation implementing full Article 12(4) minimum log set. Does that solve logging mandate for lab's own systems? It validates middleware handles high-throughput without degrading latency, gives sales artifact. It may contribute to solution but is it solving logging mandate for their own R&D? It's a demo not necessarily production deployment for all high-risk systems. Might be partial solution. Effectiveness 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution of problem (it helps, but only partial). Could be 4? It gives reference for client conversations, validates middleware. But does it meet logging mandate for lab's own R&D? Maybe not fully solve. I'd say 3.\n\napplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\nSolves an identified problem directly related: do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem. Building reference implementation addresses Article 12 logging mandate. Applicable directly. Level 4? Could be 3 solves implied problem. The stated problem is how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Building demo is directly related. I'd say 4.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably output JSON or lines.\n\nProvide evidence one sentence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\noriginality_evidence: The proposal describes a standard compliance reference demo built for sales, which is a familiar industry practice rather than an ingenious or surprising approach. Score 2\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: It adds a demo container and audit dashboard but ke