logging practice. Could be 2. Or is it paradigm preserving? Standard compliance practice is budgeting. Might be 1 = standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way unchanged. Hmm.\n\nThe proposal introduces cost category in every project budget, makes recurring cost visible at planning stage. That's a process change but still within standard compliance management. Probably paradigm preserving? It doesn't change relationship between R&D and compliance obligations, just makes cost visible. I'd say 1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working is unchanged (just budgeting).\n\nBut could be slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. The budget line is a new element. Maybe 2.\n\nThe anchor says 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. That's exactly this. So 2.\n\nLet's pick 2.\n\nNow need output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence one sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nOrder: effectiveness, applicability, acceptability, implementability, originality, paradigm_relatedness\n\nProvide evidence sentence then score.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft:\n\neffectiveness_evidence: The line-item makes record-keeping costs explicit and prevents budget overruns, but it does not itself build logging capabilities required by Article 12.\nScore 3\n\napplicability_evidence: It addresses the implied resource-planning aspect of responding to the logging mandate rather than the technical logging requirement itself.\nScore 3 (or 4?). I'll go with 3.\n\nacceptability_evidence: Adding a mandatory budget field for compliance costs is a routine financial control that violates no legal or professional norms.\nScore 4\n\nimplementability_evidence: The finance office can add a field to an existing template and PIs can estimate hours and storage each quarter with minimal change.\nScore 4\n\noriginality_evidence: Requiring a compliance cost line in project budgets is a common, mundane management practice in regulated R&D.\nScore 1\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: It introduces a budgeting process element while still treating compliance as separate logging practice without altering how R&D is conducted.\nScore 2\n\nReturn JSON? Probably just lines. Instruction says return rating echoing its id. Provide each.\n\nI'll output structured.\n\n",
