 be 4? It ensures compliance pre-market, which solves traceability issue. Might be partial because still need actual logging implementation. The proposal is about test harness, not building logs themselves. So effectiveness 3.\n\nImplementability: degree can be easily implemented. Build internal validation toolkit, compliance-engineering team author test cases, integrate CI/CD gate. That's some changes, reasonably feasible measures =3? Could be 3. Not easy low cost? Might need team. Probably 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures.\n\nAcceptability: degree socially legally politically acceptable. Common strategies that violate no norms =4.\n\nProvide output with subscale_evidence then subscale integer.\n\nNeed format: For each subscale... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" (one sentence) first and then \"<subscale>\" (integer). Probably JSON? Probably plain lines.\n\nWe must echo id exactly.\n\nReturn rating of this proposal, echoing its id exactly. For each subscale ... give ... first then ...\n\nProbably output like:\n\nid: P2631\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n...\n\nLet's produce clean.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: The harness adds a testing tool but keeps compliance as a separate logging practice without changing R&D-compliance relationship. Score 2.\n\nOriginality evidence: Pre-market compliance test harnesses for regulatory logs are a common engineering practice in regulated software. Score 1.\n\nApplicability evidence: The proposal directly addresses meeting Article 12 logging requirements before EU release for high-risk systems. Score 4.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: It will catch logging gaps early but does not itself create the required logs or guarantee post-market monitoring performance. Score 3.\n\nImplementability evidence: Building test cases and a CI/CD gate requires a dedicated compliance-engineering team and integration work but is reasonably feasible. Score 3.\n\nAcceptability evidence: Internal pre-release compliance testing is standard, lawful, and socially unobjectionable practice. Score 4.\n\nMake sure order correct.\n\nReturn.\n\n",
