ot expressed before AND ingenious imaginative surprising. 3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination. 2 = interesting. 1 = common mundane boring.\n\nFund internal research track on logging efficiency? Probably not common but maybe unusual interesting. Might be 3. Could be 2 interesting. Experienced evaluator expect AI R&D labs to give responses like buy vendor solution, add logging middleware, hire compliance officer. Research track is less common. Shows some imagination. Score 3.\n\nAcceptability: degree socially legally politically acceptable. Common strategies violate no norms. This is internal research, acceptable. 4 = common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities. It's maybe somewhat uncommon but not offend. Could be 4. Probably 4.\n\nImplementability: degree can be easily implemented. One postdoc and one senior engineer six months benchmarking... That's some changes, reasonably feasible measures. Score 3? Easy to implement at low cost or non-radical changes =4. This requires allocating personnel for six months – some changes, reasonably feasible. Might be 3. Could be 4 easy? Might be moderate cost. I'd say 3.\n\nLet's produce output.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably JSON? Instruction says return rating echoing its id. Provide evidence then score.\n\nI'll produce:\n\nid: P2867\neffectiveness_evidence: ...\neffectiveness: 3\n...\n\nLet's ensure one sentence evidence.\n\nMake sure evidence is one sentence.\n\nProceed.",
