ncing? Probably common, mundane. It's a standard financial control. Originality 1 = common, mundane, boring.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm.\nParadigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working is unchanged. Ring-fence budget is still treats compliance as logging practice, introduces new element (cost centre) but still treats compliance as logging practice? Definition: 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. 1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working is unchanged.\n\nRing-fencing budget is a standard management practice, not changing relationship between R&D and compliance obligations. Probably paradigm preserving =1. Could be slightly stretching? Introduces new element (budget line). But still treats compliance as logging practice. Might be 2? The definition says slightly paradigm stretching introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. A budget line is a process. Hmm.\n\nI'd say paradigm preserving: standard compliance practice; lab way unchanged. Score 1.\n\nAcceptability (1-4): degree to which idea is socially, legally, politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies that violate no norms. 4 = common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities. Budget ring-fencing is acceptable. Score 4.\n\nImplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\nEasy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes? Creating a budget line requires finance office approval but is reasonably feasible. Might be some changes, reasonably feasible. Could be 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Or 4 easy to implement at low cost? Carving out 8% of R&D envelope is significant change. Probably not trivial. I'd say 3.\n\nLet's output with evidence sentences then score.\n\nNeed format: